# Survey – generated by the "question‑me" skill

## Round 1

```survey-json
{
  "round": 1,
  "generatedAt": "2026-11-23T08:19:26.000Z",
  "stage": "question-me",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "How big may one 'run finished' report (the complete-execution POST) be before the backend refuses it? We need ONE number that both the backend's accepted size limit and the runner's packing budget are based on.",
      "options": [
        "5 MiB",
        "10 MiB (the value suggested in the task brief)",
        "16 MiB",
        "32 MiB"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "If a report is STILL too large and the backend answers '413 Payload Too Large', what should the runner do? (The requirement is: never crash, never loop — but the exact 'report once as failed' behaviour needs your call.)",
      "options": [
        "Send one small 'failed' report instead (task files left out, exact byte size in the failure reason), then stop — never send the big report again",
        "Send no second report at all; just release the task with an interrupt whose reason contains the size details, then stop",
        "Retry the full big report exactly once more, then give up"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "Task folders can contain binary files (for example PNG screenshots). When the runner packs the task files into the report, what should happen to those binaries?",
      "options": [
        "Skip all common binary types entirely (images, PDFs, archives, and similar)",
        "Skip only image files (PNG / JPG / GIF / WebP); ship everything else as today",
        "Keep images but downsample / compress them so they stay small"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "After binaries are handled, how much total room should the task files have inside the report (the cap in collectTaskFiles, which today is 1 MiB total + 256 KiB per file)?",
      "options": [
        "Keep roughly today's 1 MiB total for files, but subtract headroom for the ~20 KiB output and the JSON wrapping so the whole envelope fits",
        "Scale the file cap up to most of the agreed backend limit from q1 (limit minus output minus JSON overhead)",
        "No total cap at all once binaries are excluded — rely only on the per-file 256 KiB cap"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q5",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "Which backend routes should get the raised size limit from q1? (The plan only names the complete-execution route; the new test api/bodyLimit.default.test.js is meant to pin that everything else keeps Fastify's 1 MiB default.)",
      "options": [
        "Only the runner's complete-execution route; every other route keeps the 1 MiB default",
        "All runner-to-backend routes (complete-execution, logs, log-events, progress, heartbeat, …)",
        "The whole API, app-wide (not recommended — removes the default protection everywhere)"
      ],
      "required": false,
      "showIf": null
    }
  ],
  "answers": {
    "q1": {
      "selected": [
        "10 MiB (the value suggested in the task brief)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q2": {
      "selected": [
        "Send one small 'failed' report instead (task files left out, exact byte size in the failure reason), then stop — never send the big report again"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q3": {
      "selected": [
        "Skip all common binary types entirely (images, PDFs, archives, and similar)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q4": {
      "selected": [
        "Scale the file cap up to most of the agreed backend limit from q1 (limit minus output minus JSON overhead)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q5": {
      "selected": [
        "All runner-to-backend routes (complete-execution, logs, log-events, progress, heartbeat, …)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    }
  }
}
